---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
		<title>Talks — Olivia Fjord Sloth</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Book Olivia Fjord Sloth for talks about adventure, curiosity, mistakes and the stories that came out of them." />
	</head>

	<body>
		<SiteHeader />

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">STORIES TOLD OUT LOUD</p>
				<h1>Stories worth leaving the sofa for.</h1>
				<p class="intro">
					From solo journeys through places shaped by conflict to a very unlikely route
					from struggling in school to a PhD in physics. Two different talks, both built
					around curiosity, mistakes and the stories that came out of them.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="talks">

				<article class="talk-card">
					<div class="talk-image">
						<img src="/tur2.webp" alt="Olivia Fjord Sloth travelling in the mountains" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>

					<div class="talk-content">
						<p class="number">01</p>
						<p class="label">ADVENTURE & OUTDOOR</p>

						<h2>Hiking in the Shadows</h2>

						<p class="subtitle">
							What happens when you walk through places most of us only know from the news?
						</p>

						<p>
							I travel slowly, often alone and often on foot. Some of those journeys have taken
							me through Central Asia, Iran, Lebanon, Iraqi Kurdistan and Syria — places we mostly
							hear about when something goes wrong.
						</p>

						<p>
							In this talk, I share stories from mountains, caves, border areas and long days on foot:
							accepting invitations from strangers, getting caught near demonstrations, navigating
							military checkpoints and ending up in situations I could never have planned.
						</p>

						<p>
							But travelling this way also raises questions. How much should you trust?
							When does curiosity become irresponsibility? And what does it mean to be a guest
							in a place shaped by conflict?
						</p>

						<p>
							It is a talk about hospitality, risk, vulnerability and the people you meet when
							you slow down enough to let the journey change along the way.
						</p>
						<p class="good-for">
							<strong>Good for:</strong> libraries, outdoor clubs, højskoler, associations,
							cultural venues and companies.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>


				<article class="talk-card reverse">
					<div class="talk-image">
						<img src="/te_speak.webp" alt="Olivia Fjord Sloth giving a talk" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
					</div>

					<div class="talk-content">
						<p class="number">02</p>
						<p class="label">SCHOOLS & YOUNG PEOPLE</p>

						<h2>Choosing Curiosity Over the Fear of Failure</h2>

						<p class="subtitle">
							From “not suited for high school” to circus school,
							 back to the classroom - and eventually a PhD in physics.						</p>

						<p>
							I was told I wasn’t suited for high school. I was dyslexic, struggled in school
							and definitely didn’t imagine that I would one day end up with a PhD in physics.
						</p>

						<p>
							My way there wasn’t particularly straight. I went to circus school, spent some
							time away from traditional education and eventually found my way back to the
							classroom.
						</p>

						<p>
							This talk is about that slightly messy road — but also about adventure,
							travelling and what can happen when curiosity becomes more important
							than the fear of getting things wrong.
						</p>

						<p>
							Whether that means going back to school, travelling alone somewhere unfamiliar
							or simply trying something you are not sure you can do, the point is not to stop
							being afraid of failure — but to become curious enough to try anyway.
						</p>

						<p>
							The talk can be adapted to the age of the students and the setting.
						</p>

					<p class="good-for">
						<strong>Good for:</strong> schools, youth programmes, universities,
						folk high schools and other educational settings.
					</p>
					</div>
				</article>

			</section>

			<section class="experience">
				<p class="label">EXPERIENCE</p>
				<p>
					I’ve spoken to audiences ranging from efterskole students to PhD students,
					as well as at libraries and public events.
				</p>
			</section>

			
			<section class="details">
				<div>
					<p class="label">FORMAT</p>
					<p>Talk, break and Q&A</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">LANGUAGE</p>
					<p>Danish or English</p>
				</div>

				<div>
					<p class="label">CUSTOM</p>
					<p>Both talks can be adapted to the audience and event.</p>
				</div>
			</section>


			<section class="booking">
				<p class="label">BOOK A TALK</p>

				<h2>Interested in booking a talk?</h2>

				<p>
					Send me a message with a little about the audience, the event and which talk you are interested in.
				</p>

				<a href="mailto:oliviasloth@hotmail.com">Get in touch →</a>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>


<style>
	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html,
	body {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		background: #f4f1ea;
		color: #171717;
	}

	body {
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
	}

	header {
		padding: 30px 48px;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.name {
		font-size: 22px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
	}

	nav {
		display: flex;
		gap: 32px;
	}

	nav a {
		font-size: 15px;
	}

	nav .active {
		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
	}

	main {
		padding-bottom: 120px;
	}

	.hero {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 100px auto 140px;
		padding: 0 48px;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.label {
		margin: 0 0 20px;
		font-size: 11px;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		max-width: 1050px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(64px, 8vw, 125px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 0.94;
		letter-spacing: -0.04em;
	}

	.intro {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 45px 0 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(24px, 2.7vw, 36px);
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: #555;
	}

	.talks {
		max-width: 1400px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 48px;
	}

	.talk-card {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 80px;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0 0 150px;
	}

	.talk-card.reverse .talk-image {
		order: 2;
	}

	.talk-card.reverse .talk-content {
		order: 1;
	}

	.talk-image img {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.talk-content {
		max-width: 620px;
	}

	.number {
		margin: 0 0 10px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 24px;
		color: #777;
	}

	.talk-content h2 {
		margin: 0 0 26px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(42px, 4.5vw, 68px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.02;
		letter-spacing: -0.025em;
	}

	.subtitle {
		margin: 0 0 32px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 25px;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: #555;
	}

	.talk-content > p:not(.label):not(.number):not(.subtitle) {
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.good-for {
		margin-top: 30px;
		font-family: Arial, sans-serif !important;
		font-size: 15px !important;
		line-height: 1.6 !important;
	}

	.experience {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto 60px;
		padding: 0 48px;
	}

	.experience > p:not(.label) {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.details {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 55px 48px;
		border-top: 1px solid #b9b3a9;
		border-bottom: 1px solid #b9b3a9;

		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 70px;
	}

	.details p:not(.label) {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 20px;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.booking {
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 110px 48px 140px;
	}

	.booking h2 {
		max-width: 700px;
		margin: 0 0 28px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: clamp(42px, 4.5vw, 64px);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.05;
	}

	.booking p:not(.label) {
		max-width: 600px;
		font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
		font-size: 20px;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.booking a {
		display: inline-block;
		margin-top: 22px;
		padding-bottom: 4px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid #171717;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	@media (max-width: 800px) {
		header {
			padding: 24px 20px;
		}

		.name {
			font-size: 17px;
		}

		nav {
			gap: 14px;
		}

		nav a {
			font-size: 13px;
		}

		.hero {
			margin: 65px auto 90px;
			padding: 0 24px;
		}

		.hero h1 {
			font-size: 58px;
		}

		.intro {
			font-size: 24px;
		}

		.talks {
			padding: 0 24px;
		}

		.talk-card,
		.talk-card.reverse {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 45px;
			padding-bottom: 100px;
		}

		.talk-card.reverse .talk-image,
		.talk-card.reverse .talk-content {
			order: initial;
		}

		.talk-image {
			order: -1;
		}

		.talk-content h2 {
			font-size: 44px;
		}

		.subtitle {
			font-size: 22px;
		}

		.talk-content > p:not(.label):not(.number):not(.subtitle) {
			font-size: 18px;
		}
		.experience {
			margin-bottom: 70px;
			padding: 0 24px;
		}
		.details {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			padding: 55px 24px;
			gap: 40px;
		}

		.booking {
			margin-top: 80px;
			padding: 0 24px;
		}
	}
</style>
